From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] SystemUI: the clock shows AM/PM when it is a 12-hour clock

The status bar clock and the one in quick settings leave out AM/PM (Clock's
amPmStyle defaults to gone): on the device (Test V40) at 22:42 the only clock
on the screen read "10:42". A phone has a lock screen or a widget with the
whole time; here it is the only one, so a 12-hour clock now shows it in full,
"下午10:42" or "10:42 PM", in the clock's own size, 14 sp (the small style,
0.7 of it, is below 12 sp, the smallest for a short label in
docs/design/eink-ui.md, rule 8).

Whether the clock is 12- or 24-hour is unchanged: the language's convention
until the user sets "Use 24-hour format" in Settings. A 24-hour clock has no
AM/PM to show.

--- a/packages/SystemUI/res/layout/status_bar.xml
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/res/layout/status_bar.xml
@@ -75,6 +75,7 @@
                 android:paddingStart="@dimen/status_bar_clock_starting_padding"
                 android:paddingEnd="@dimen/status_bar_clock_end_padding"
                 android:gravity="center_vertical|start"
+                systemui:amPmStyle="normal"
                 />
         </com.android.keyguard.AlphaOptimizedLinearLayout>
     </LinearLayout>
--- a/packages/SystemUI/res/layout/quick_status_bar_header_system_icons.xml
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/res/layout/quick_status_bar_header_system_icons.xml
@@ -55,5 +55,6 @@
         android:paddingEnd="@dimen/status_bar_clock_end_padding"
         android:gravity="center_vertical|start"
         systemui:showDark="false"
+        systemui:amPmStyle="normal"
         />
 </LinearLayout>
